// S~S  SimpleSal signal starts  S~S

[Managing App+ssTEA Configurations.note]    search in app-fsmDemo source files for a reference to this file.

   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   A complex configuration may be established on a per-App basis, or, shared by several similar Apps.
   That configuration can then be shared by every member of the team working on the same App(s).
   No changes to the ss_configuration.h file should be necessary while enabling/disabling features.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   For a Simple Sal App project, the configuration may evolve and stabilize as development evolves;
   the definition of a version at a point in Time is best contained in the App, not in a shared file.
   Propagating changes to the configuration over time as Apps emerge is a software engineering task.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   This creates a duplication of similar or dissimilar configurations across Apps or pressure to
   conform to the configuration established as the trustworthy baseline.  This is the driving force
   for placing the specification of the configuration in the App: change and variation management.
   The App(s) can manage the complexity using build options such as this example; outside SimpleSal.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// S~S  SimpleSal signal ends  S~S
